text:
anya: FYI from today's onboarding load test: when the browser sampleapp fan-outs 12 parallel page requests we see synchronized retries after 429s and duplicated embed work + cost noise. anyone have quick ideas other than 'reduce parallelism'?
carlos: seen it. classic fanout-stampede. SDK backoff respects Retry-After but the retries all align because workers don't coordinate session state.
mike: can you paste a tiny header trace? wondering if server can help more than Retry-After.
anya: short trace:
```
POST /v1/embeds/batch 180ms
<- 429 Retry-After: 1
<- X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
<- body: {"code":"rate_limit","phase":"ingest"}
```
anya: client waits 1s, then 12 workers retry nearly simultaneously. result: server accepts ~3 and 9 get 429 again.
emily: two layers of fix: client coordination + server advisory headers. client: attach a per-session sequencer (shared across workers) so only N concurrent inflight per session; server: return an advisory X-Queue-Index or X-Session-Backoff hint to help stagger.
carlos: parity bug note: JS SDK's jitter RNG sometimes reuses seed across web workers -> near-zero jitter. fix RNG and add a small entropy sanity check.
mike: sample fix for the client-side sequencer (very small, put in sampleapp libs):
```js
// per-session semaphore
const sessionSem = makeSemaphore({max: 4});
async function sendBatch(sessionId, batch) {
  await sessionSem.acquire();
  try {
    return await sdk.embed(batch);
  } finally {
    sessionSem.release();
  }
}
```
This keeps each logical session bounded.
emily: alternative lightweight approach: a per-session token-bucket in front of the SDK; if token unavailable, wait random(30,200)ms then retry acquire. smoother than blocking.
carlos: also we could have server include X-Backoff-Multiplier: 1.7 and X-Queue-Index: 7 so clients add multiplier to base backoff and add an offset proportional to queue index * small jitter. that avoids synchronized retries.
mike: telemetry: emit metric when session sees >5 retries in 60s and tag as sampleapp/onboard. we can alert and find customers hitting stampede.
ci-bot: New issue created: INF-4512 "client fanout stagger + per-session inflight controls" assigned to @carlos @emily :white_check_mark:
emily: i'll add a short doc section describing two recommended client patterns (semaphore slow-start and token-bucket stagger) and a tiny sampleapp helper lib. i'll also sketch server advisory header formats.
carlos: i'll add maxInFlightPerSession config to all SDKs with default 4 for onboarding templates and add an e2e that simulates 12 parallel workers asserting duplicate accept rate <1.6x.
anya: short-term: sampleapp maintainers can flip to the sem/token-bucket helper. long-term: server headers + SDK telemetry. thanks all. :thumbsup:
